---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";

const seo = {
  title: "Scryer | woflo",
  description:
    "An exact mathematical engine for agentic research: deterministic mathematical semantics underneath stochastic search.",
  image: "/images/social-card.png",
};
---

<Layout seo={seo}>
  <article class="mt-8 content-section scryer-page">
    <header class="mb-[var(--space-xl)] scryer-header">
      <div class="scryer-title-wrap">
        <h1 class="page-title">Scryer</h1>
        <span class="scryer-title-scratch" aria-hidden="true">f(x) = ? &nbsp;→&nbsp; exact</span>
      </div>
      <p class="scryer-tagline">exact mathematics for systems that guess.</p>
    </header>

    <div class="prose prose-invert prose-a:text-[var(--chromatic-cyan)] prose-a:underline-offset-4 prose-headings:mb-2 prose-p:opacity-85 scryer-note">
      <p>Models are good at guessing what might be true. Scryer gives those guesses somewhere exact to land. It's a symbolic engine for research: it works over exact mathematical objects, derives what it can, and says where it gets stuck. Some results come with evidence you can replay.</p>

      <section class="scryer-section" aria-labelledby="why-heading">
        <span class="scryer-margin-note" aria-hidden="true">P(x) ? ≠ ⊢P(x)<br /><i>[not the same]</i> ↓</span>
        <h2 id="why-heading">why</h2>
        <p>A model can notice a pattern or choose a useful next question. Its confidence shouldn't do the algebra.</p>
        <figure class="scryer-loop">
          <div class="scryer-loop-track">
            <div class="scryer-loop-node">
              <span class="scryer-loop-index">01 / guess</span>
              <strong>agent</strong>
              <span>chooses what to try</span>
            </div>
            <svg class="scryer-loop-arrow" viewBox="0 0 56 22" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path class="scryer-loop-flow" d="M2 11H49" /><path class="scryer-loop-tip" d="m43 5 6 6-6 6" /></svg>
            <div class="scryer-loop-node scryer-loop-engine">
              <span class="scryer-loop-index">02 / work</span>
              <strong>Scryer</strong>
              <span>exact objects &amp; operations</span>
            </div>
            <svg class="scryer-loop-arrow" viewBox="0 0 56 22" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path class="scryer-loop-flow" d="M2 11H49" /><path class="scryer-loop-tip" d="m43 5 6 6-6 6" /></svg>
            <div class="scryer-loop-node scryer-loop-result">
              <span class="scryer-loop-index">03 / result</span>
              <strong>established</strong>
              <span>or still open, with a reason</span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <figcaption>Both outcomes can inform the next guess, but only established results become facts.</figcaption>
        </figure>
      </section>

      <div class="scryer-derivation scryer-number-train" aria-hidden="true">
        <span><b>01</b> ? <em>[hunch]</em></span><i>···→</i><span><b>02</b> 𝒳</span><i>···→</i><span><b>03</b> ≡ <em>[same?]</em></span><i>···→</i><span><b>04</b> ⊢ <em>[checked]</em></span>
      </div>

      <section class="scryer-section" aria-labelledby="exists-heading">
        <span class="scryer-margin-note" aria-hidden="true">f(a) = g(b) ?<br /><i>[collision]</i></span>
        <h2 id="exists-heading">what exists now</h2>
        <p>It works with rationals and algebraic numbers, fields, polynomials, matrices, logic, graphs, optimisation, dynamics, and other domains.</p>
        <p>Ask what follows from an object, or work backwards from laws to objects that satisfy them.</p>
        <p>A generic construction space can reach the same mathematical object by different routes. That collision gives an identity to inspect.</p>
        <p>Scryer can also search for candidate relations and counterexamples, and keep track of open conjectures.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="scryer-section" aria-labelledby="in-use-heading">
        <h2 id="in-use-heading">a few outputs</h2>
        <p>These screenshots come from an artifact made for this page. Scryer handles the calculations; the artifact reader draws the plots.</p>
        <div class="scryer-gallery" role="region" aria-label="Scryer mathematical readings" tabindex="0">
          <figure class="scryer-shot">
            <a href="/images/scryer/octave-curve.webp" aria-label="Open the octave curve and value table at full size">
              <img src="/images/scryer/octave-curve.webp" alt="Scryer reading f sub n = 440 times 2 to the n over 12: a plotted curve and a table with exact values 440, 880, and 1760 at n = 0, 12, and 24" width="864" height="2480" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
            </a>
            <figcaption>frequency curve · 440, 880 and 1760 Hz at n = 0, 12 and 24.</figcaption>
          </figure>
          <figure class="scryer-shot">
            <a href="/images/scryer/piecewise-curve.webp" aria-label="Open the piecewise curve screenshot at full size">
              <img src="/images/scryer/piecewise-curve.webp" alt="Scryer reading a piecewise function: t squared for t at most one and two minus t above one, with both curves meeting at one" width="864" height="1168" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
            </a>
            <figcaption>piecewise rule · the branches meet at t = 1.</figcaption>
          </figure>
          <figure class="scryer-shot">
            <a href="/images/scryer/complex-roots.webp" aria-label="Open the complex roots screenshot at full size">
              <img src="/images/scryer/complex-roots.webp" alt="Scryer returns the exact roots three plus or minus two i for x squared minus six x plus thirteen equals zero; the artifact reader plots the conjugate pair" width="864" height="1080" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
            </a>
            <figcaption>complex roots · 3 ± 2i.</figcaption>
          </figure>
        </div>
      </section>

      <div class="scryer-derivation scryer-fork" aria-hidden="true">
        <span class="scryer-fork-start">φ</span>
        <span class="scryer-fork-line">── ? ──┬──→ ⊢ φ <em>[keep]</em></span>
        <span class="scryer-fork-branch">└──→ ∃x : ¬φ(x) <em>[one bad x]</em></span>
      </div>

      <section class="scryer-section" aria-labelledby="rule-heading">
        <span class="scryer-margin-note scryer-margin-note-red" aria-hidden="true">⊬ φ<br /><i>[leave open]</i></span>
        <h2 id="rule-heading">the important rule</h2>
        <p>Scryer can say no.</p>
        <p>If it runs out of search budget, lacks the right representation, or needs mathematics it doesn't have, the result should say so. An unproved claim stays unproved.</p>
        <p>An exact calculation can still start from faulty assumptions or answer the wrong question. Those limits should stay visible.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="scryer-section" aria-labelledby="direction-heading">
        <h2 id="direction-heading">where it's headed</h2>
        <p>Verification came first. The work now is to let an agent build exact objects, search through them, and use what it finds to choose its next question.</p>
        <p>A small proof and search system is testing that idea. Suggestions can steer the search. Only checked results are treated as facts; an open goal still shows what needs proving.</p>
      </section>

      <div class="scryer-derivation scryer-loop-note" aria-hidden="true">
        <span>?</span><i>→</i><span>𝒳</span><i>→</i><span>⊢</span><i>↘</i><span>•</span>
        <small>↖&#xFE0E; &nbsp; ?′ <em>[again]</em> &nbsp; ─────────┘</small>
      </div>

      <section class="scryer-section" aria-labelledby="example-heading">
        <h2 id="example-heading">a tiny example of the idea</h2>
        <p>The search recovered the familiar identity <span class="scryer-equation">√(3 + 2√2) = 1 + √2</span> when two constructions reached the same exact number.</p>
        <div class="scryer-equation-chain" aria-hidden="true">
          <span>1 + √2</span><i>(·)²</i><span>3 + 2√2</span><i>√·</i><span>1 + √2 <em>[same]</em></span>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section id="use" class="scryer-section" aria-labelledby="use-heading">
        <h2 id="use-heading">use it</h2>
        <p>Public research access runs through Stithy, which serves Scryer as MCP tools for agents.</p>
        <p><a href="/projects/#scryer-access">Public research access details and bearer keys →</a></p>
      </section>

      <section class="scryer-section" aria-labelledby="underneath-heading">
        <span class="scryer-margin-note" aria-hidden="true">φ → n₁ → n₂<br />↺ <i>[replay]</i></span>
        <h2 id="underneath-heading">underneath</h2>
        <p>The engine works with distinct mathematical structures that share arithmetic machinery. Each domain adds its own rules. Where implemented, certificates and proof DAGs make results replayable.</p>
        <p>When one of those results looks odd, there's a trail to follow.</p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>

<style>
  .scryer-page {
    --scryer-ink: var(--chromatic-cyan);
    overflow: visible;
  }

  .scryer-header {
    position: relative;
  }

  .scryer-title-wrap {
    position: relative;
    display: inline-block;
    isolation: isolate;
  }

  .scryer-title-scratch {
    position: absolute;
    z-index: -1;
    top: 48%;
    left: 72%;
    width: max-content;
    color: rgb(var(--scryer-ink) / 0.15);
    font-family: var(--font-casual);
    font-size: clamp(1rem, 4cqi, 1.45rem);
    font-weight: 400;
    letter-spacing: 0.025em;
    line-height: 1;
    transform: rotate(-4deg);
    pointer-events: none;
    user-select: none;
  }

  .scryer-tagline {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: var(--text-lg);
    opacity: 0.65;
  }

  .scryer-note {
    max-width: 72ch;
  }

  .scryer-section {
    position: relative;
  }

  .scryer-margin-note {
    position: absolute;
    top: 0.4rem;
    right: clamp(-10.5rem, -13vw, -7rem);
    width: 8.5rem;
    color: rgb(var(--scryer-ink) / 0.16);
    font-family: var(--font-casual);
    font-size: 0.92rem;
    font-weight: 400;
    letter-spacing: 0.02em;
    line-height: 1.15;
    text-align: center;
    transform: rotate(-4deg);
    pointer-events: none;
    user-select: none;
  }

  .scryer-section:nth-of-type(even) .scryer-margin-note {
    transform: rotate(3deg);
  }

  .scryer-margin-note i,
  .scryer-derivation em,
  .scryer-equation-chain em {
    color: rgb(var(--color-text-rgb) / 0.3);
    font-family: var(--font-casual);
    font-size: 0.88em;
    font-style: normal;
    font-weight: 400;
    letter-spacing: 0.015em;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  .scryer-margin-note i {
    color: inherit;
    opacity: 0.72;
  }

  .scryer-equation {
    position: relative;
    padding-inline: 0.12em;
    color: rgb(var(--color-text-rgb) / 0.94);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.94em;
    font-weight: 500;
    box-shadow: inset 0 -1px rgb(var(--scryer-ink) / 0.26);
    box-decoration-break: clone;
    -webkit-box-decoration-break: clone;
  }

  .scryer-derivation,
  .scryer-equation-chain {
    color: rgb(var(--scryer-ink) / 0.44);
    font-family: var(--font-casual);
    font-weight: 400;
    pointer-events: none;
    user-select: none;
  }

  .scryer-derivation {
    width: min(100%, 39rem);
    margin: -0.2rem 0 2.35rem;
    padding: 0.2rem 0.35rem 0.15rem;
    border-bottom: 1px dashed rgb(var(--scryer-ink) / 0.1);
    font-size: clamp(0.78rem, 2.1cqi, 0.9rem);
    line-height: 1.35;
    transform: rotate(-0.35deg);
  }

  .scryer-number-train {
    display: flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 0.45rem;
  }

  .scryer-number-train span {
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  .scryer-number-train b {
    margin-right: 0.18rem;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.72em;
    font-weight: 400;
    opacity: 0.72;
  }

  .scryer-number-train i,
  .scryer-loop-note i {
    color: rgb(var(--scryer-ink) / 0.26);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-style: normal;
  }

  .scryer-fork {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: max-content 1fr;
    gap: 0 0.55rem;
    width: min(27rem, 88%);
    margin-left: auto;
    transform: rotate(0.7deg);
  }

  .scryer-fork-start {
    grid-row: 1 / span 2;
    align-self: center;
  }

  .scryer-fork-line,
  .scryer-fork-branch {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.8em;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  .scryer-fork-branch {
    color: rgb(var(--chromatic-red) / 0.34);
  }

  .scryer-loop-note {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(7, max-content);
    align-items: baseline;
    justify-content: end;
    gap: 0.45rem;
    width: min(31rem, 92%);
    margin-left: auto;
    transform: rotate(-0.8deg);
  }

  .scryer-loop-note small {
    grid-column: 2 / -1;
    justify-self: center;
    color: rgb(var(--scryer-ink) / 0.27);
    font-size: 0.82em;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
  }

  .scryer-equation-chain {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: max-content minmax(2.8rem, 1fr) max-content minmax(2.8rem, 1fr) max-content;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.45rem;
    margin: 1.15rem 0 1.75rem;
    font-size: clamp(0.82rem, 2.25cqi, 0.96rem);
    transform: rotate(-0.45deg);
  }

  .scryer-equation-chain span {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    color: rgb(var(--color-text-rgb) / 0.64);
  }

  .scryer-equation-chain i {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.35rem;
    font-style: normal;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  .scryer-equation-chain i::before,
  .scryer-equation-chain i::after {
    content: "";
    height: 1px;
    flex: 1;
    background: rgb(var(--scryer-ink) / 0.22);
  }

  .scryer-equation-chain i::after {
    clip-path: polygon(0 0, 100% 50%, 0 100%);
    width: 0.35rem;
    flex: 0 0 0.35rem;
    height: 0.35rem;
    background: rgb(var(--scryer-ink) / 0.32);
  }

  .scryer-margin-note-red {
    color: rgb(var(--chromatic-red) / 0.2);
  }

  .scryer-loop {
    margin: var(--space-md) 0 var(--space-lg);
    padding: var(--space-sm) 0;
    border-block: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  }

  .scryer-loop-track {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) 3rem minmax(0, 1.15fr) 3rem minmax(0, 1.15fr);
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--space-xs);
  }

  .scryer-loop-node {
    display: flex;
    min-width: 0;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.2rem;
    padding-left: var(--space-xs);
    border-left: 1px solid rgb(var(--color-text-rgb) / 0.45);
  }

  .scryer-loop-engine {
    border-left-color: rgb(var(--chromatic-cyan) / 0.8);
  }

  .scryer-loop-index {
    color: rgb(var(--color-text-rgb) / 0.7);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .scryer-loop-node strong {
    color: var(--color-text);
    font-size: var(--text-base);
    line-height: 1.2;
  }

  .scryer-loop-node > span:last-child {
    color: rgb(var(--color-text-rgb) / 0.78);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    line-height: 1.4;
  }

  .scryer-loop-arrow {
    width: 100%;
    overflow: visible;
    fill: none;
    stroke: rgb(var(--chromatic-cyan) / 0.65);
    stroke-width: 1.5;
    stroke-linecap: round;
    stroke-linejoin: round;
  }

  .scryer-loop-flow {
    stroke-dasharray: 3 5;
    animation: scryer-flow 1.8s linear infinite;
  }

  .scryer-loop figcaption {
    margin-top: var(--space-sm);
    color: rgb(var(--color-text-rgb) / 0.75);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  @keyframes scryer-flow {
    to { stroke-dashoffset: -8; }
  }

  .scryer-gallery {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: var(--space-sm);
    align-items: start;
    padding: var(--space-xs) 0;
  }

  .scryer-gallery:focus-visible {
    outline: 2px solid rgb(var(--color-text-rgb) / var(--opacity-focus));
    outline-offset: 2px;
  }

  .scryer-shot {
    min-width: 0;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .scryer-shot:first-child {
    grid-row: span 2;
  }

  .scryer-shot a {
    display: block;
    overflow: hidden;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    cursor: zoom-in;
  }

  .scryer-shot img {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .scryer-shot figcaption {
    margin-top: var(--space-xs);
    color: rgb(var(--color-text-rgb) / 0.75);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  @media (max-width: 40rem) {
    .scryer-title-scratch {
      left: 58%;
      opacity: 0.82;
    }

    .scryer-loop-track {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
      gap: 0;
    }

    .scryer-loop-arrow {
      width: 3rem;
      height: 1.5rem;
      margin: 0.65rem 0 0.65rem 0.35rem;
      transform: rotate(90deg);
    }

    .scryer-derivation {
      width: 100%;
      margin-bottom: 2rem;
      font-size: 0.74rem;
    }

    .scryer-number-train {
      gap: 0.2rem;
    }

    .scryer-fork,
    .scryer-loop-note {
      width: 100%;
      margin-left: 0;
    }

    .scryer-loop-note {
      justify-content: start;
      gap: 0.28rem;
    }

    .scryer-equation-chain {
      gap: 0.25rem;
      font-size: 0.72rem;
    }

    .scryer-gallery {
      display: flex;
      overflow-x: auto;
      overscroll-behavior-inline: contain;
      scroll-snap-type: x mandatory;
      padding-bottom: var(--space-sm);
      scrollbar-color: var(--color-border) transparent;
    }

    .scryer-shot {
      flex: 0 0 min(78vw, 18rem);
      scroll-snap-align: start;
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 68rem) {
    .scryer-margin-note {
      display: none;
    }
  }

  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .scryer-loop-flow { animation: none; }
  }
</style>
